-- title:
--   Automorphisms of the Γ₀(M')-fibre datum over a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)\,M'$ (the subfield of `LaurentSeries (ResidueField A)` generated over the residue field of $A$ by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`) over that residue field, and let `hW` assert that the members of $W$ are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. exactly the places $w$ with `IsSupersingularPlace q M' (ResidueField A) w`. Let `hle` be the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the first being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the second $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)\,M'$: a valuation subring `integers` of the characteristic-zero field, a surjective ring homomorphism `residue` onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal of `integers`, a map `placeMap` on places, together with the compatibilities required by that structure (membership over $A$, compatibility with $A$-constants, the scaling property, preservation of degrees of places and the divisor-pushforward identity). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue`, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally, let $s$ be one of the places in $W$, hence a supersingular place.
--
--   For the small field: let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$ (`hπ`), and write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that it is a henselian local ring; `hres`, that its residue field is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$.
--
--   For the auxiliary level: let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell' \neq q$, $\ell' \ge 3$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), normalised by `hιξ`, which provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, required by `hK` to equal the base change to $k_0$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')$, the level being the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$. Let $j$ be a non-zero element of $K$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ is the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion `jq` (`hj`).
--
--   Two equivariance hypotheses govern level structures over $A_0$-algebras: `hℓ` states that for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$ over $T$, if $D$ is an $\ell'$-level-$P$ structure on $W$ then $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ is one on $C \bullet W$; `hM` states the corresponding assertion for `IsGamma0PowAt`, the transported polynomial being $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\,C\,(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k)\,h$. Further, $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras with unit discriminant, subject to `h𝒢` (chord–tangent: the law is computed by a points evaluation) and `h𝒢O` (the origin is the identity, witnessed by a section of the origin chart with vanishing $x/y$ and $z/y$); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` together with `h𝒯`, the assertion that its variable-change and base-change actions transport the two Drinfeld sections correctly through the induced maps of projective models. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` supply, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms of the models realising a variable change ($\mathrm{IsVariableChangeHom}$) respectively a coefficient homomorphism along an $A_0$-algebra map ($\mathrm{IsCoefficientHom}$), each dominating the irrelevant ideal in the stated sense.
--
--   Write $\mathcal R = \mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h\ell\,hM\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ for the rigid Weierstrass datum whose level object has three components: the $\Gamma_0$-power kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$ (`level.1`), an $\ell'$-level-$P$ datum (`level.2.1`) and a Drinfeld pair of level $q$ (`level.2.2`). Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$, i.e. an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point `univ` such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra is the image of `univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map. Let $x_0$ be a point of that datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant, read in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$, is $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$ (`hx₀`). Let $\mathrm{clC} : B_0 \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ be an $A_0$-algebra map into the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,K\,\{j\} \subseteq K$, which by `hclC` becomes the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$ after inclusion into $K$.
--
--   The Tate-point hypothesis `hμ` asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ and of a raw point $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ with six properties: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; the coefficients of $C$ satisfy $u \cdot \bigl(2(\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[1,0])_1 + \tfrac16\bigr) = 2(\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[1,0])_2 + (\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[1,0])_1$, $r = -\tfrac1{12}$, $s = -\tfrac12$, $t = \tfrac1{24}$ (the last four as constant Hahn series, with $\xi$ made a unit by `hξ`); the curve of $r$, pushed to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$, equals $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$; for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ pushed to $F'$ equals $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$ applied to $C$ (pushed by $f$), to $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,v_p(M')$ and to $\prod_a (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^a)_1)$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; the $\ell'$-level datum $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ pushes to $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[q,0]\,[0,-q]).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; and there are $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images are the four coordinates of $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[\ell',0]\,[0,-\ell']).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ and with $\mathrm{IsSectionThrough}$ holding for the two Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ at $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the following. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ and let $\psi$ be an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism from that algebra to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$ whose vanishing set is exactly $y$ (for all $c$, $\psi c = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$). Assume that $y$ lies over $s$ in the following sense: for every $g \in \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ belonging to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$ (cusp-regularity relative to $j$), and such that the $R_0$-residue of that element lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: whenever $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ of the coefficient embedding of $g$ lies in $K$ and the resulting element lies in the chart algebra, and whenever $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ satisfies $\mathrm{residue}\,A\,c = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, then the difference of that chart element and the image of $c$ under $A_0 \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ lies in $y$. Then for every raw point $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$ whose class in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}$ equals the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under the map induced by $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$,
--   $$\#\{\,C : \mathrm{VariableChange}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0) \ \mid\ (\mathcal R.\mathrm{act}\,C\,x).\mathrm{curve} = x.\mathrm{curve} \ \text{and} \ (\mathcal R.\mathrm{act}\,C\,x).\mathrm{level}.1 = x.\mathrm{level}.1 \,\} = 2 \cdot \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s,$$
--   the cardinality being `Nat.card` of the subtype so described, and $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ being by definition the natural-number quotient of $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ evaluated at $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M')$ by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$. Only the Weierstrass model and the $\Gamma_0$-power component of the level object are required to be fixed; the $\ell'$-level-$P$ datum and the Drinfeld pair are not constrained in the count.
--
--   This is the automorphism count attached to the fibre of the rigid level-$q\ell'$ chart over a supersingular place $s$: the variable changes fixing the Weierstrass model and the cyclic $M'$-kernel polynomials of the reduced point number exactly twice the width character of $s$, which is the moduli-theoretic count of automorphisms of an elliptic curve with cyclic $M'$-structure in characteristic $q$. It feeds the construction of the supersingular fibre dictionary, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssFibreDictionary_autCount_chartAlgFin_rigidDataPow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssFibreDictionary_autCount_chartAlgFin_rigidDataPow), in the analysis of the reduction of modular curves at $q$.
